{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":23119033,"ns":0,"title":"Application-layer framing","extract":"Application-layer framing or application-level framing (ALF)  is a method of allowing  an application to use its semantics for the design of its network protocols.\nThis procedure was first proposed by D. D. Clark and David L. Tennenhouse.","description":"Protocols constructed at the application layer","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}